[{:seon.task/name "a-form-has-a-time-bound"
  :seon.task/plan "`seon.turn/act!` evaluates through `seon.repl/eval-string` with no per-form bound, so a model's infinite loop holds its attempt forever. Correct: a config key bounds a form, passed in act!; the interrupt is the named failure point `seon.intr/run` (docs/failure-points.md), and the interrupted form is recorded."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.turn-test/an-endless-form-is-interrupted-and-recorded}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-turn-records-what-it-saw-and-spent"
  :seon.task/plan "A turn records its `:seon.turn/basis` and `:seon.turn/split` (`seon.turn/basis!`), but not the model's raw reply, its finish_reason, model and reasoning, nor the whole split as the agent saw it (4-15 s gaps in a real run had to be traced by hand). Correct: per turn, the messages sent are derivable from the basis; the reply's finish_reason, model and reasoning, and the split context render / model round trip / evals / record / tests are recorded. The dashboard's agent page shows the recorded context, not a second producer of it."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.turn-test/a-turn-records-its-context-reply-and-time-split}} {:seon.task/name "an-outside-context-is-the-turns-context"
  :seon.task/plan "`seon.turn/context-block` (the server's read of a task for an outside worktree session) now takes the attempt's plan and `seon.turn/observe`'s gaps since the branch's merge base (`seon.merge/uncontracted`), as the turn loop does, so main's pre-existing contract gaps are no longer charged to the agent. It still passes turn n of max-turns 1 to `seon.turn/basis!`, so the context says \"turn 1 of 1\" while the attempt's env says 8. Correct: context-block passes the attempt's env max-turns, so the outside session reads exactly what the turn loop's model would. Replaces the second set of basis arguments; nothing new."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.turn-test/an-outside-context-names-only-the-branchs-own-gaps}}]
